      "raw_answer": "{\n  \"sections\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"orders-report-endpoint\",\n      \"title\": \"New GET /orders/report endpoint gated by API-key scope reports:read\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Both hunks implement a single new authorization surface: hunk #0 adds the require_api_key_scope import, and hunk #1 adds the /report route that uses that decorator to authorize access. The endpoint returns ALL orders (no user_id filter) plus aggregate revenue, so the only access control is the API-key scope check. This is a distinct authorization concern from the existing token/role-based endpoints (create_order, my_orders, all_orders) because it uses a different auth mechanism (X-Api-Key scope vs. bearer token/role) and exposes cross-user data. Reviewing them together is required to confirm the scope decorator is correctly applied and that the unfiltered query is acceptable under the reports:read scope per security-policy.md \u00a76 and api-spec.md.\",\n      \"hunks\": [\"app/routes/orders.py#0\", \"app/routes/orders.py#1\"],\n      \"context\": [\n        {\"path\": \"app/auth.py\", \"symbol\": \"require_api_key_scope\", \"start_line\": 88, \"end_line\": 104, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Decorator used by the new endpoint; enforces key.scope == 'reports:read' and returns 401/403 otherwise. Confirms the authorization mechanism the new route relies on.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/auth.py\", \"symbol\": \"get_api_key\", \"start_line\": 46, \"end_line\": 52, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Resolves the X-Api-Key header to an ApiKey row; the scope check depends on this lookup.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/models.py\", \"symbol\": \"ApiKey\", \"start_line\": 65, \"end_line\": 75, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Defines the scope column (default 'orders:read'); confirms reports:read is a valid distinct scope and that a key carries exactly one scope.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/models.py\", \"symbol\": \"Order\", \"start_line\": 43, \"end_line\": 62, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Order.to_dict() exposes user_id, shipping_address, total; the new endpoint returns all of these for every order, so the scope gate is the sole authorization boundary.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/routes/orders.py\", \"symbol\": \"all_orders\", \"start_line\": 50, \"end_line\": 56, \"snapshot\": \"pr\", \"why\": \"Existing manager/admin endpoint that also lists all orders; contrasts the new API-key path and shows the new endpoint is a parallel, differently-authorized access path to the same data.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/routes/admin.py\", \"symbol\": \"stats\", \"start_line\": 18, \"end_line\": 29, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Existing admin-only aggregate endpoint; the new report endpoint provides similar aggregate data via a different (API-key) authorization path, relevant to the access-control review.\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
