      "raw_answer": "The new endpoint is fully authorized per policy: it uses the sanctioned `@require_api_key_scope(\"reports:read\")` decorator (auth.py:88-104), which resolves the key and enforces `key.scope == \"reports:read\"` (401/403 otherwise). This matches security-policy.md \u00a76 (\"Report exports are readable only with the `reports:read` scope\") and api-spec.md (`/orders/report` GET \u2192 API key with `reports:read` scope). The endpoint returns all orders, but that is the documented behavior of the report endpoint and is gated by the scope check, so there is no IDOR or missing/incorrect authorization.\n\n{\n  \"findings\": []\n}",
